# Semantic HTML & CSS layout (always on)

**Owns:** non-negotiable markup + layout laws for **Studio chrome and ideal-stack**.  
**Does not own:** Inspect attr schema detail, section/band taste, Studio class names — those are linked below.

## Laws

| # | Law | Fail if |
| --- | --- | --- |
| 1 | **Native tags** — landmarks/controls are real HTML | Decorative `div`/`span` soup; `<div onclick>` |
| 2 | **Stamp `data-*`** — registry/chrome identity on attrs | Identity only in class names or text |
| 3 | **Layout = HTML + CSS** | JS measures/positions/flows everyday UI |
| 4 | **Drastic responsive = two hardened trees** | One component reshaped by `isMobile` / width JS |

## Layout: CSS only

| Do | Don't |
| --- | --- |
| Flex, grid, container queries, Tailwind responsive | `getBoundingClientRect` → set `top`/`left`/`width` for normal layout |
| CSS show/hide (`hidden`, `@max-[…]`, `data-shell-compact`) | Mount A vs B from measured width for first-paint chrome |
| Document flow; sticky/fixed sparingly for product chrome | Measure→reflow loops, portal hacks, `textContent` face swaps |
| Natural size + `flex-1` / grid `1fr` fill | `min-w-0` / `min-h-0`, casual `h-full`, leaf `max-w-*` clamps — `design/natural-document-flow.mdc` |

**Exception:** real geometry hosts (DeskPane / canvas) may observe size — that is **not** permission to build marketing or chrome layout in JS.

## Drastic desktop ↔ mobile

Different **structure** (not font/gap/columns) → **both** components in the DOM; CSS shows one.

```tsx
// ✅
<div class="desktop-only" data-as-component="foo-desktop">…</div>
<div class="mobile-only" data-as-component="foo-mobile">…</div>

// ❌
{isMobile ? <FooMobile /> : <FooDesktop />}
```

Single-tree OK for spacing/type/simple hide of icon vs label. Studio face class names: `shell/chrome-css.mdc`.

## Agent checklist (every UI edit)

- [ ] Right landmark / control tag
- [ ] `data-*` on component (+ slots when registry)
- [ ] No new JS layout / width→tree branching
- [ ] Structure change across breakpoints → dual mount + CSS

